---
/*
 * Editorial, not another centred hero. The headline holds the left of a 12
 * column grid and the supporting copy sits offset from it — lower and to the
 * right — so the two read in sequence rather than as one stacked block.
 *
 * White and compact. It follows the footage hero as an editorial change of
 * pace rather than another screen-sized statement.
 */
---

<section id="why-hood" class="section bg-surface">
  <div class="container-page">
    <span class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Why HOOD</span>

    <div class="mt-2.5 grid gap-x-16 gap-y-7 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-y-0">
      {/* The cap is a different measure at each end, because the size is. At
          27px on a 335px column a 17ch cap runs the line to the gutter, and at
          52px a 13ch one stacks the same sentence four lines deep. Neither
          number is right at the other size. */}
      <h2 class="h-section max-w-[20ch] lg:col-span-7 lg:max-w-[17ch]" data-reveal style="--reveal-i:1">
        Your community already has enough to manage.
      </h2>

      {/*
        The offset. On desktop this column starts partway down the headline
        beside it, which is what stops the two from reading as a centred
        stack; the rule is the only thing marking where the copy begins, and
        on a phone it does that work on its own.

        The drop is measured against the headline, not chosen for its own
        sake. Now that the headline sets to two tight lines rather than three
        loose ones, the old 7.5rem left the bottom-left of the section empty
        enough to read as a hole instead of as asymmetry.
      */}
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 lg:col-start-8 lg:mt-10" data-reveal style="--reveal-i:2">
        <span class="block h-px w-16 bg-brand-red" aria-hidden="true"></span>

        <p class="mt-4 max-w-[46ch] text-[17px] font-medium leading-[1.55] lg:text-[18px]">
          Pools need to be staffed. Common areas need attention. Small
          maintenance and cleanup jobs still have to get handled.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 max-w-[46ch] text-[16px] leading-[1.6] text-muted lg:text-[17px]">
          HOOD Community Services helps HOAs handle the everyday work that keeps
          a community running. From pool staffing and management to cleanups,
          hauling, power washing, and other community needs, we’re here to make
          those responsibilities easier to manage.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
